.TH UGPIBD-PORTMAP 1 "August 2026" "ugpibd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ugpibd\-portmap \- portmapper advertising ugpibd's VXI-11 core channel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ugpibd\-portmap
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-core\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fixed-table ONC-RPC portmapper (RFC 1833) answering
.BR GETPORT ,
.BR DUMP ,
and
.B NULL
for ugpibd's VXI-11 core channel, over both TCP and UDP.
It exists for VISA stacks that discover VXI-11 instruments via the
portmapper (NI, Keysight) and for
.BR rpcinfo (8).
pyvisa-py does not need it: its resource strings carry the port
(\fBTCPIP::host,9010::gpib0,23::INSTR\fR).
.PP
.B SET
and
.B UNSET
are refused (the table is fixed at startup), and
.B CALLIT
is answered with silence per RFC 1833 \(sc3.2, as no UDP programs are
registered.
.PP
The mode is chosen automatically at startup by probing localhost:111:
.TP
.B register mode
A portmapper already answers (rpcbind \(em Debian and Raspberry Pi OS
install it by default). The core channel is registered with it via
PMAPPROC_SET, exactly as classic ONC-RPC services announce themselves;
rpcbind keeps port 111. The process stays resident, re-registering if
rpcbind's table is reset (a restart wipes it) and withdrawing the
registration on shutdown.
.TP
.B serve mode
Nobody answers on port 111: bind it and serve GETPORT/DUMP/NULL directly.
The systemd unit grants CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for this.
.PP
One unit, one command:
.B systemctl enable --now ugpibd-portmap
\(em no operator mode decision.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B register
Register program 395183 (tcp, \fB\-\-core\-port\fR) with the portmapper at
127.0.0.1:\fB\-\-port\fR and exit.
.TP
.B unregister
Withdraw that registration and exit.
.PP
With no subcommand, serve the portmap protocol directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-bind " " \fIADDR\fR
Bind address (default 127.0.0.1). Must match where clients reach the
daemon: GETPORT answers with a port only, the host being the one asked.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Portmap port (default 111, which needs privileges to bind directly).
.TP
.BR \-\-core\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
The port advertised for the VXI-11 core channel; must match the daemon's
\fB\-\-vxi11\-port\fR (default 9010).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity (repeatable).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ugpibd (1),
.BR rpcinfo (8)
